      <h4 style="font-size: 10pt; margin-top: 15px;">Principle of operation</h4>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The ring sensors with a bistable switching action picks up the relay in the amplifier when the ball float reaches the trigger level and remains in that position, even if the float continues to move towards the alarm zone, thus leaving the trigger level. The relay will drop out as soon as the float crosses the trigger level from the opposite direction, and moves back from the alarm zone into the normal operating range. The actual float position above or below the trigger level - is precisely indicated.</p>
